# Testing and verification

- Read `.cursor/rules.md` before changing matching files.
- Use TDD for behavior: write one failing test, confirm the expected failure, then implement minimally.
- Do not add behavior without first observing its test fail.
- Prefer real behavior over mocks; mock only external system boundaries.
- Keep unit/component tests colocated and browser journeys under `tests/e2e`.
- Run focused tests during development: `npm test -- <path>`.
- Before handoff run `npm test`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint` and `npm run build`.
- Run `npm run test:e2e` when browser behavior or release scope is involved.
- Report exact commands, exit status and any warnings; never claim success from stale output.
